 \fR\fP \fR\fP
.SH "ESLint JavaScript Plugin"
.PP
\fRWebsite\fP | \fRConfigure ESLint\fP | \fRRules\fP | \fRContribute to ESLint\fP | \fRReport Bugs\fP | \fRCode of Conduct\fP | \fRX\fP | \fRDiscord\fP | \fRMastodon\fP | \fRBluesky\fP

.PP
The beginnings of separating out JavaScript-specific functionality from ESLint\&.

.PP
Right now, this plugin contains two configurations:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRrecommended\fP - enables the rules recommended by the ESLint team (the replacement for \fR"eslint:recommended"\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRall\fP - enables all ESLint rules (the replacement for \fR"eslint:all"\fP)
.PP
.SS "Installation"
You can install ESLint using npm or other package managers:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install eslint \-D
# or
yarn add eslint \-D
# or
pnpm install eslint \-D
# or
bun add eslint \-D
.fi
.PP

.PP
Then install this plugin:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install @eslint/js \-D
# or
yarn add @eslint/js \-D
# or
pnpm install @eslint/js \-D
# or
bun add @eslint/js \-D
.fi
.PP
.SS "Usage"
Use in your \fReslint\&.config\&.js\fP file anytime you want to extend one of the configs:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { defineConfig } from "eslint/config";
import js from "@eslint/js";

export default defineConfig([
    // apply recommended rules to JS files
    {
        name: "your\-project/recommended\-rules",
        files: ["**/*\&.js"],
        plugins: {
            js,
        },
        extends: ["js/recommended"],
    },

    // apply recommended rules to JS files with an override
    {
        name: "your\-project/recommended\-rules\-with\-override",
        files: ["**/*\&.js"],
        plugins: {
            js,
        },
        extends: ["js/recommended"],
        rules: {
            "no\-unused\-vars": "warn",
        },
    },

    // apply all rules to JS files
    {
        name: "your\-project/all\-rules",
        files: ["**/*\&.js"],
        plugins: {
            js,
        },
        extends: ["js/all"],
        rules: {
            "no\-unused\-vars": "warn",
        },
    },
]);
.fi
.PP
